  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 150 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nUpper level ridging across the region Sunday will begin to break \ndown across the Northern Plans by Monday (Labor Day) as the upper \ntrough moves in. High temperatures each day will continue to remain \nwell above normal (10 to 15 degrees above), from 90 to near 95. \nPWATs will increase some during this time with chance POPs Sunday \nafternoon and Sunday night and again Monday afternoon and Monday \nnight. NBM 24 hours probability of exceeding 0.25 inch ending 12Z \nMonday increases to 40 to 50 percent across the Sandhills into North \ncentral NE, and 12Z Tuesday, from 35 to 45 percent across southwest \nNe into the eastern half of north central NE. Given the potential\nfor slow moving thunderstorms, some localized heavy rainfall is\npossible.\n\nThe upper trough is forecast to flatten out by next Tuesday and \nWednesday as an upper trough moves into the Great Lakes. This may \nbring some relief from the heat with highs from 85 to around 90. \nChances for precipitation look low as surface high pressure settles \ninto the region. By next Thursday, upper ridging is favored to build \nback in.",
